From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 11:53:57 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/vkms: allow the stereo modes of the EDID

With an EDID whose HDMI Vendor-Specific Data Block declares 3D (HDMI
1.4b, section 8.3.2 and Appendix H), the EDID parser lists the frame
packing, top and bottom and side by side modes the sink declares, and
every other structure of HDMI 1.4a on the formats that carry it. The
probe helper then drops each of them with MODE_NO_STEREO, because
drm_mode_validate_stereo() keeps a stereo mode only on a connector with
stereo_allowed and VKMS never set it. A guest on the published kernels
read the EDID through configfs and listed the 2D modes only.

The composer and the writeback connector handle the frame of every
layout now, so set stereo_allowed on every VKMS connector, as i915,
nouveau, amdgpu, vc4 and virtio-gpu do for their HDMI connectors.
Connectors without an EDID are unchanged: drm_add_modes_noedid() adds no
stereo mode. Frame-sequential modes keep their own opt-in.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/vkms/vkms_connector.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/vkms/vkms_connector.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/vkms/vkms_connector.c
index f456c62..770edf1 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/vkms/vkms_connector.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/vkms/vkms_connector.c
@@ -128,6 +128,9 @@ struct vkms_connector *vkms_connector_init(struct vkms_device *vkmsdev,
 
 	drm_connector_helper_add(&connector->base, &vkms_conn_helper_funcs);
 
+	/* The composer and writeback handle the frame of every stereo layout, see vkms_frame_size() */
+	connector->base.stereo_allowed = true;
+
 	/* The output alternates the eyes and names them, see vkms_crtc_handle_vblank_timeout() */
 	connector->base.stereo_frame_sequential_allowed =
 		vkms_config_connector_get_stereo_frame_sequential(connector_cfg);
